From d1f462e4bd1b1c14f83c1cbd6e85dda0ca680888 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 00:28:54 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 22/43] test(chexc): sections 5-6 -- unconditional clauses,
 effects axis, assumption scope

- parse/flagoff_clause_inert.cj replaces flagoff_clause_rejected.cj: with checking off the
  clauses parse and impose nothing, which is the rule the old test pinned the opposite of.
- performs/performs_without_chexc.cj -- a missing handler is an error with only the
  effect-handler feature enabled, while a 'throws' clause in the same file imposes nothing.
- performs/performs_dots_neg.cj -- the '...' marker on a 'performs' clause.
- types/captures_command.cj -- commands in a 'captures' clause: in scope in a receiver body,
  required at the construction site.
- types/clause_unchecked_bound_neg.cj -- a type parameter bounded by an unchecked type.
- assume/assume_package_scope_neg.cj (+ its support file) -- the annotation in one file, the
  call in another, which is the discriminating case for package versus file scope.
- assume/assume_empty_neg.cj -- '@AssumeThrows[]'.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
